 * Core question: What share of assessed stocks are fished at biologically unsustainable
 * levels, and is that share still rising?
 *
 * Primary vintage: FAO The State of World Fisheries and Aquaculture 2024 (SOFIA),
 * stock-status reference year 2021 on the fixed ~445-stock assessment panel
 * (~72% of global marine capture landings). Secondary contrast: FAO Review of the
 * state of world marine fishery resources 2025 (2,570 stocks) ??? different census,
 * not a drop-in replacement for the SOFIA time series.
 */

export type Confidence = "disclosed" | "approx-chart" | "derived";

