  "Stock-status shares from FAO SOFIA 2024 (reference year 2021) on FAO???s long-run assessed-stock panel. Unsustainable = overfished (biomass below the level that can produce MSY). Sustainable = maximally sustainably fished + underfished. Area percentages are sustainable-stock shares by FAO Major Fishing Area; unsustainable = 100 ??? sustainable. Production-weighted landings shares treat larger stocks more heavily than equal-stock counts. 2025 Review figures (64.5% sustainable / 35.5% overfished on 2,570 stocks) are a broader census, not spliced into the 1974???2021 SOFIA path.";

